# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of the checkout
# platform's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Several scripts under scripts/ were found checked out with CRLF line
# endings (a `\r` trailing every line, including the shebang). A `\r`
# immediately after `#!/bin/bash` on a script invoked via AWS SSM
# (scripts/incident-scenarios.sh, invoked by sentinel-ai's chaos-scenario
# runner) or by CI can make the interpreter path in the shebang fail to
# resolve, causing the whole script to fail to execute rather than merely
# running slowly. bash also rejects CRLF-corrupted `function() {` headers
# outright under `bash -n`. This file prevents the corruption from
# recurring on a future Windows/OneDrive checkout; it has no effect until
# this directory is (or becomes) a git repository.
*.sh text eol=lf
